From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:24:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: make no frames while the front end is halted

DirectSound halts the APU front end for a moment to edit voice lists.
The frame thread kept making monitor-only frames meanwhile, so each halt
was a gap of silence as long as the halt (0.4-2.4% of frames in a level).
xemu makes none and lets its output queue carry the sound; so does this
now (only when the software mixer and test tone are idle). The pipeline
catches up on the resume, paced by the device queue.

Arctic Antics attract demo, 56 s: dropouts 13 -> 0, clicks 81 -> 6
(with the seam fix); hub sliding, 30 s: dropouts 3 -> 0. Underruns 0.

Local change approved by the user (notes 18.49), never pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/apu/apu_core.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/apu/apu_core.c b/src/apu/apu_core.c
index 5dd8a93..809578c 100644
--- a/src/apu/apu_core.c
+++ b/src/apu/apu_core.c
@@ -510,6 +510,17 @@ static void *mcpx_apu_frame_thread(void *arg)
         if (apu_active && !g_test_tone.active) {
             /* Full pipeline: VP voices → DSP → monitor → waveOut */
             se_frame(d);
+        } else if (xcntmode != NV_PAPU_SECTL_XCNTMODE_OFF &&
+                   !g_test_tone.active && !g_mixer_active_count) {
+            /* Halted: DirectSound stops the front end for a moment to edit
+             * voice lists. Making frames here made each halt a gap of
+             * silence as long as the halt (0.4-2.4% of frames in a level).
+             * xemu makes none and lets its output queue carry the sound;
+             * so does this: the device plays what is queued (up to
+             * THROTTLE_QUEUE_TARGET frames) and the pipeline catches up on
+             * the resume. A halt longer than the queue is still an
+             * underrun, counted on the [APU-OUT] line (notes 18.49). */
+            qemu_cond_timedwait(&d->cond, &d->lock, 1);
         } else {
             /* Lightweight: just monitor frame (test tone + software mixer) */
             mcpx_apu_monitor_frame(d);
